1
00:07:21,428 --> 00:07:27,428
A night that changed her life became a scandal that rocked a nation.

2
00:14:42,857 --> 00:14:48,857
Black Box Diaries is a documentary film directed by Shiori Ito.

3
00:22:04,285 --> 00:22:10,285
Journalist Shiori Ito embarks on a courageous investigation of her own sexual
assault in an improbable attempt to prosecute her high-profile offender.

4
00:29:25,714 --> 00:29:31,714
Her quest becomes a landmark case in Japan, exposing the
country's outdated judicial and societal systems.

5
00:36:47,142 --> 00:36:53,142
Self, played by Shiori Ito.

6
00:44:08,571 --> 00:44:14,571
Self (archive footage), played by Noriyuki Yamaguchi.

7
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:36,000
Self (archive footage), played by Shinzo Abe.

8
00:58:51,428 --> 00:58:57,428
Black Box Diaries (Japanese: ブラック・ボックス・ダイアリーズ, romanized: Burakku Bokkusu
Daiarīzu) is a 2024 documentary film directed by Shiori Itō.

9
01:06:12,857 --> 01:06:18,857
The film chronicles her investigation into her own sexual assault case.

10
01:13:34,285 --> 01:13:40,285
The film premiered at the 2024 Sundance Film Festival.

11
01:20:55,714 --> 01:21:01,714
It was released in the United States and United Kingdom on October 25,
2024, by MTV Documentary Films and Dogwoof, respectively.

12
01:28:17,142 --> 01:28:23,142
The film was named one of the top 5 documentary films of 2024 by the National Board of Review, won a
Peabody Award, and was nominated for Best Documentary Feature Film in the 97th Academy Awards.

13
01:35:38,571 --> 01:35:44,571
The film explores themes of japan, sexual violence,
justice, human rights, female journalist.
